It is an unofficial Rust port of the rules engine of Unciv
(https://github.com/yairm210/Unciv), an open-source remake of Civilization V
by Yair Morgenstern and the Unciv contributors, licensed under the Mozilla
Public License, v. 2.0. crates/civ-core reimplements Unciv's rules with
Unciv's Kotlin source as the reference, and parts of it are close ports; it is
treated as a Modification of Unciv's Covered Software under MPL-2.0. The following are mechanical transforms of Unciv source or
output and carry the same terms:

  crates/civ-core/src/unique_type.rs        from UniqueType.kt
  crates/civ-core/src/generated/api.rs      from logic/multiplayer/apiv2/*.kt
  crates/civ-core/src/generated/assets.rs   sprite names from Unciv's atlases
  crates/civ-core/src/ruleset/generated.rs  from Unciv's ruleset JSON schema
  crates/civ-core/tests/data/unciv_*.json   values computed by Unciv

Unciv's Civ V rulesets ("Civ V - Gods & Kings", "Civ V - Vanilla") are used
as test fixtures but are not included in this repository: their names and
texts derive from Civilization V. crates/civ-core/tools/fetch_unciv_rulesets.sh
downloads them from Unciv at a pinned commit. The rulesets this project ships,
crates/civ-core/rules/base and crates/civ-core/rules/blitz, are its own.

